A||N||4||Zzaaak||No fuel presure problem, 87 Fiero GT ||||1
Z||000000||Zzaaak||10-02-1999||05:05 AM||||Ok I am getting no fule presure.  But the fuel pump works fine when I hot wire the relay.  After i hot wire the relay the car still won't start.  It used to run a month earlier.   But it would spit a sputter at low rpm's and run fine above 1500 rpms.  But it also has a total loss of power when I try to drive it up hills.   Anyway a month later it would just start up and immediatly die.  I discovered No Fuel presure..... But the chilton manuel I bought it terrible.  The diagnostic comes out  No Fuel Presure.  Yet it gives you no Ideas on what to fix or replace. And it still won't run when the pump is hot wired.  And it used to run a month before..... So any ideas on what it might be.  Thanks<BR>Zak||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||10-02-1999||11:18 AM||||Fiero fuel injected engines require a certain amount of fuel pressure to operate. If the pressure drops below the amount needed, the engine won't run. A old worn out fuel pump may still work, but just not have enough fuel pressure.<P>First thing though, replace the fuel filter. If cars sit around and don't get driven regularly, gunk builds up in the gas tank and will get sucked up into the filter. If the filter is clogged enough, fuel pressure drops and again, the engine won't run.<P>Also, check the fuel lines for damage, maybe one got bent up or clogged. Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dan||10-02-1999||11:20 AM|||| Sounds like a fuel pump going bad. Oh, its located in the fuel tank.Try to get a pressure reading with a gage on the pressure side  fuel line.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Zzaaak||10-02-1999||01:20 PM||||Thanks for the suggestions.... I did goto the library looked through all the Michel Shop manuels, got a copy of all diagrams and diagnosis flow charts.  This first thing I plan to do is check my relay, then the fuel presure. Another unusual thing is the Oil presure skyrockets to the max when the car starts up then it might go down a little bit.  But it is pretty spuratic.<BR>Thanks<BR>Zak||||reg||1
Z||000004||Zzaaak||10-03-1999||08:34 PM||||Turns out it was a bad fuel pump... Learned my best lesson in fuel injection so far.  Your car will spitter and sputter if you have bad fuel presure.  Problem solved and the car runs great now.  Thanks for the help.<BR>It had 18 psi fuel presure when I tested it... Follow a cool diagnostic flow chart and got the answer to my problem... ||||reg||6
